The condition `New_Ret >= 0 && Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount` ensures that if the return value (`New_Ret`) is non-negative, the old and new list count will be the same. This is what the comment is saying. 

Please note that running this code will result in an AssertionException at runtime if the condition is not met. This is because the `Debug.Assert` statement is designed to help developers to find bugs in their code, specifically in situations where conditions are unexpected based on the normal flow of the software. Therefore, this code should be used more for development and debugging purposes rather than for an actual test suite to validate the ArrayList.
